  "rules": "Probe policy: s_t = predicted P(S_t) from the probe at loop t (t in 1..3); halt at the first t with s_t >= threshold, else loop 4. Failed questions have s_t = -inf (run 4 loops, wrong), as in Gate 1. Grid, operating-point rule and tie-breaks are exactly Gate 1's (gate1.grid_thresholds / gate1.select_point with kind native_gate: ties -> smaller loss, then the largest threshold). Probe choice: among 3 families x {h, hx}, largest validation operating-point saving; ties -> smaller validation loss -> simpler (family 1<2<3, h<hx); unqualified configs cannot be chosen.",
  "baseline_rules": "Grid: 50 thresholds = np.quantile(values, np.linspace(0, 1, 50)), values = the statistic pooled over all validation questions of the benchmark set (ok questions only) and loops 1..3 (deployable_kl: D over its 3 columns); exact repeated thresholds are removed keeping order. Qualified point: macro validation loss <= 1.0 percentage point (+1e-12). Selection among qualified points: maximize macro validation saving; ties (1e-12) broken by smaller macro validation loss; remaining ties broken by the most conservative threshold (confidence, native_gate: largest; entropy, deployable_kl: smallest). A baseline with no qualified point is not qualified. fixed-k has one point each. Macro = unweighted mean over benchmarks. Thresholded policies halt at the earliest loop t in {1,2,3} whose rule fires, else run to loop 4. deployable_kl pays for loop t+1 and answers with loop t+1.",
